openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/specs/standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/spec.md:9:For a supported ball-valve tender query that explicitly states standard execution or standard passage, the system SHALL produce at most one distinct additive retrieval representation that retains every source term and adds catalog-native standard-bore vocabulary. The source tender text SHALL remain the authoritative query for original retrieval, reranking, result text, and duplicate-query caching.
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/specs/standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/spec.md:12:- **WHEN** a supported ball-valve tender includes an explicit standard-execution phrase and does not request a conflicting bore type
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/specs/standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/spec.md:13:- **THEN** the system provides a distinct additive retrieval representation containing standard-bore vocabulary while preserving the original tender query
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/specs/standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/spec.md:17:- **THEN** the system provides an additive representation that preserves the stated requirement and normalizes it to the catalog-native standard-bore vocabulary
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/specs/standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/spec.md:21:The system SHALL NOT infer standard bore from generic standard wording outside an explicit supported ball-valve execution or passage context. It SHALL NOT add standard-bore vocabulary for another product family, unsupported/no-product text, or a query that explicitly requests full or reduced bore.
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/specs/standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/spec.md:23:#### Scenario: Generic standard wording is not a bore requirement
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/specs/standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/spec.md:25:- **THEN** the system does not add standard-bore vocabulary on the basis of that wording
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/specs/standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/spec.md:29:- **THEN** the system preserves that query's existing retrieval representation and does not add standard-bore vocabulary
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/specs/standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/spec.md:33:The system SHALL use the standard-bore representation only as an additional retrieval input through the existing bounded hybrid-retrieval path. It SHALL retain original-query candidates if alternate retrieval is unavailable or errors, and it SHALL not duplicate an LD product solely because it was retrieved through both representations.
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/specs/standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/spec.md:36:- **WHEN** retrieval of a standard-bore alternate fails after original-query retrieval succeeds
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/design.md:3:See `proposal.md` for the experiment motivation. The existing pure retrieval canonicalizer already returns a normalized source query plus at most one alternate, and hybrid retrieval searches both representations, deduplicates each modality by LD id, and applies existing RRF once per modality. The matcher sends the original source query, not the alternate, to DeepSeek reranking. The harness calibration recognizes explicit standard ball-valve execution as a standard-bore requirement, and catalog product text can express that requirement as `стандартнопроходной` or `стандартный проход`.
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/design.md:24:Extend the existing canonicalization boundary only when the query contains a supported ball-valve anchor and an explicit standard-execution or standard-passage phrase. Add the catalog lexical variants `стандартнопроходной` and `стандартный проход` to the existing canonical text rather than replacing source wording. Before emitting the alternate, detect explicit full-passage or reduced-passage wording and decline the standard-bore expansion if either is present.
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/design.md:26:This is preferred to treating every `стандартн*` token as a synonym: that broader rule would change requirements for unrelated products and conflicts with the outcome of the earlier broad shorthand experiment. It also avoids an LLM rewrite, which could infer unmentioned technical properties.
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/design.md:37:- [A query contains contradictory full/reduced-bore language] → Treat the conflict as ineligible for standard-bore expansion and retain existing canonicalization only.
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/design.md:43:1. Add the pure, guarded standard-bore lexical expansion to the existing canonicalization flow.
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/tasks.md:1:## 1. Guarded standard-bore canonicalization
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/tasks.md:3:- [x] 1.1 Extend the pure retrieval canonicalization boundary to emit at most one distinct additive representation containing catalog-native standard-bore vocabulary only for supported ball-valve queries with explicit standard-execution or standard-passage wording; verify focused unit tests assert exact source and alternate query text for representative Russian phrase variants.
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/tasks.md:4:- [x] 1.2 Preserve all source requirements in the alternate and block the new expansion for generic standard wording, other product families, unsupported/no-product text, and explicit full- or reduced-bore wording; verify focused no-op and conflicting-requirement tests.
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/tasks.md:8:- [x] 2.1 Verify the existing hybrid retrieval path issues both original and standard-bore alternate queries only when the alternate is distinct, deduplicates candidate IDs, and retains original-query candidates after alternate-query retrieval failure; add or update mocked hybrid-retriever tests.
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/proposal.md:3:The current champion still returns a human-rejected full-bore ball valve for an explicit standard-execution request, despite the harness documenting catalog candidates with explicit standard-bore evidence. The failure is a narrow vocabulary mismatch: tender wording says `стандартное исполнение`, while catalog evidence uses standard-passage terminology. Earlier selection-adjacent experiments regressed or did not improve metrics; a bounded additive retrieval representation is the strongest remaining distinct mechanism.
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/proposal.md:7:- For supported ball-valve tender queries that explicitly state standard execution, create an additive canonical retrieval representation containing catalog-native standard-bore vocabulary.
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/proposal.md:9:- Do not infer a bore type from generic words such as `стандартный` unless they occur in an explicit ball-valve execution/passsage context; do not expand unrelated product families or explicit full/reduced-bore requests.
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/proposal.md:16:- `standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization`: Safely expands explicit standard-execution ball-valve terminology into an additive catalog-native retrieval representation.
openspec/changes/cycle-09-standard-bore-retrieval-canonicalization/proposal.md:25:- Affected behavior: hybrid candidate generation may gain an additional standard-bore representation; reranking and final selection behavior remain unchanged.

